---
import CourseLayout from '../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro';
import RomanceDebugger from '../../components/RomanceDebugger.astro';
import { withBase } from 'astro-theme-university/url';
---

<CourseLayout title="Romance Debugger" description="One conversation. Several possible actions. Only the evidence gets to change the state.">
  <p>Step into Alex’s fictional message thread. Choose an action, inspect its result, then reveal the next authored event. Sometimes the useful answer is <strong>“we don’t know yet.”</strong></p>
  <RomanceDebugger />
  <section aria-labelledby="debugger-course-links">
    <h2 id="debugger-course-links">Take the trace back to the course</h2>
    <p>This practice uses the <a href={withBase('/lectures/week-06/')}>Week 6 message decision tree</a>. It adds a local record of your choices and manually revealed events. The replies are scripted examples; a choice does not cause or predict someone’s response.</p>
    <p>In the <a href={withBase('/sessions/06-message-tree/')}>Week 6 tutorial</a>, use a trace during the existing tree exercise, then explain the same route in your pseudocode. <a href={withBase('/lectures/week-07/')}>Week 7</a> adds explicit clocks and observation windows. You can also return to the <a href={withBase('/toolkit/')}>course toolkit</a>.</p>
  </section>
</CourseLayout>
